{"id": "EUVD-2026-48885", "enisaUuid": "b61d9903-7e39-3883-964e-ca7b0e910c9f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nUSB: iowarrior: fix use-after-free on disconnect race\n\nmutex_unlock() may access the mutex structure after releasing the lock\nand therefore cannot be used to manage lifetime of objects directly\n(unlike spinlocks and refcounts). [1][2]\n\nUse a kref to release the driver data to avoid use-after-free in\nmutex_unlock() when release() races with disconnect().\n\n[1] a51749ab34d9 (\"locking/mutex: Document that mutex_unlock() is non-atomic\")\n[2] 2b9d9e0a9ba0 (\"locking/mutex: Clarify that mutex_unlock(), and most\n                   other sleeping locks, can still use the lock object\n                   after it's unlocked\")", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:50:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:16", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e7d3c98fed73d3be84d3e146d8d9be0309e725b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c0a7b29ebb391d5f50b115e86f842b709195b08", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30ec3025b771511625375fb3fb959aea3b45fb0d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71590982700fdeb39a37a500c877228b0140978e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c602254ba4c10f60a73cd99d147874f86a3f485c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jfg4-c35c-vjq6", "CVE-2026-64341"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fa023b1-4a8e-31b3-a2cb-05232ad69f7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1deea153-0a9b-3f4b-ba3a-3b1ba5252125", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "946b960d13c15f050a3b848987aaca79f6a459b7 <30ec3025b771511625375fb3fb959aea3b45fb0d"}, {"id": "5993b211-8538-3c8e-a451-7ac7b11486aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.58"}, {"id": "71a98294-4119-343e-89ca-e06653fd7501", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"